modama and Forschungszentrum Jülich, with EOSC Data Commons credited

modama runs this search for the ER-C's data, and the page says so (@weber,
2026-11-16: co-brand; keep EOSC's funding line; remove the e-INFRA CZ
acknowledgement; example queries from electron microscopy; Tools stay as they are):

- Start page: the FZJ logo top left, a link to the ER-C's page; the modama logo above
  the search instead of EOSC Data Commons', a link to this deployment's landing page
  (https://er-c-data.fz-juelich.de/, @weber 2026-11-16: it looked clickable and led
  nowhere; upstream's clicks for its easter egg go with it, its code left unused);
  three electron-microscopy example queries, which start AI Mode, not the keyword
  search (@weber 2026-11-16: "IMO the traditional search is legacy").
- Results and chat pages: modama's logo instead of EOSC's icon, and FZJ's next to it
  (on the results page only on phones and from xl, where the search bar has the room;
  the footer has it too). Profile page: modama's logo. modama.svg has much empty space
  around the word; aspect-[116/40] object-cover shows the word, as the agent GUI's
  modama-tint.svg does with that viewBox.
- Footer: FZJ's logo and the ER-C's name instead of e-INFRA CZ, whose computing this
  deployment does not use; "Search based on EOSC Data Commons matchmaker" instead of
  "Made with ❤️ in Europe"; EOSC's logo, funding line and links stay.
- The title "modama search"; FZJ's icon as the favicon.

The images are not in this patch: matchmaker.Dockerfile copies them into src/assets/
from branding/ and deploy/landingpage/ (modama.svg; fzj-logo.png from fzj_logo.jpg,
which is a PNG; fzj-favicon.ico from favicon.ico).

Left as they were: the chat's bot avatar, the conversation export (EOSC's logo and
SITE_NAME), the Tools section, the About link, the policy pages, the data player.

Applies after 0004.

